Section 2: CDealSampleExtractor — Reading Symbol, Hour, and Profit
Every deal this extractor reads gets reduced to exactly three things: which symbol it traded, what hour of the day (in UTC) it closed, and what it made or lost. There's no need to track when the position was opened, since a heatmap grouped by hour of day only cares about the moment a trade ended, not how long it was open beforehand. That keeps this reader considerably shorter than a typical deal history reader: no lookup for a matching open time, no position ID tracking, just one pass through history pulling out the fields the aggregation step actually needs.
